{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 54, :comments ["<b>And the seven years of famine began, etc., as Joseph had said.</b> It was necessary to say <b>as Joseph had said</b>, for through this his words in the interpretation of the dream were verified further. For beforehand, one might say that it was mere chance that the seven years of plenty came; but when the seven years of plenty were completed and the years of famine began, then Joseph's words were proven true." "<b>Or</b> it may intend this way: <b>And the seven years began</b>, etc. — and you will ask: how would they feel the famine perceptibly at the start of the year of famine after all the plenty, when everyone's storehouses were full of grain — would the famine not be recognized immediately? To this the verse explains: <b>as Joseph had said</b> — meaning that he had told them (Genesis 41:31): ״וְלֹא יִוָּדַע הַשָּׂבָע בָּאָרֶץ״, meaning they would eat and not be satisfied, and this matter was recognized at the start of the year."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:50.642931764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}